message: If you use this repository, please cite the manuscript.
title: "Uncertainty-Based Risk Ordering and Objective-Specific Ligand Ranking for Metal–Ligand Selectivity"
authors:
  - family-names: TBD
    given-names: TBD
type: article
license: TBD
repository-code: TBD
abstract: >
  Direct ligand-disjoint modelling of metal-metal selectivity (DS2) alongside
  absolute stability constants (DS1). A heteroscedastic MLP ensemble workhorse
  provides predictive uncertainty that orders held-out error far more effectively
  than fingerprint, descriptor-space, learned-representation, or pair-support
  distances, and objective-specific pair-acquisition ranking shows that the best
  shortlist rule depends on the experimental objective.
